  the board restarts while it is read: a running program stops and starts again. Nothing is erased or written.
  port   /dev/cu.usbmodem101
  mac    dc:da:0c:xx:xx:xx
  spark's last deploy here: none in its store record (it keeps only its own deploys)
  chip   same      esp32s3
  flash  same      16 MB
  simulation: passed
  the passed run's scenario has no set-control step (the step that presses a button or sets a sensor) and no expect-pin step (the step that reads a pin)
  what this simulation cannot show, so test it on the board:
  - ONBOARD_DISPLAY — spark adds no part to the diagram for the board's own display, so a passed run does not test what it shows. Test it on the board.
  all fields match the board record firebeetle2-esp32s3.
deploy.py: no terminal to ask you in. Run this line in your own terminal window (Claude Code's ! has none):
  SPARK_HOME=<store> <repo>/scripts/deploy.py --project <project> --token 5aed-<image> --port /dev/cu.usbmodem101
Or, to let Claude deploy this board for N minutes (1 to 1440) with no yes each time, run this once. It allows an erase of ALL of the flash and any passed image of any project:
  SPARK_HOME=<store> <repo>/scripts/grant.py --scope deploy --minutes N --project <project> --port /dev/cu.usbmodem101
